{
  "id": "62b84c0b-e2e0-4f44-a4ea-7415dcc59646",
  "title": "SC Orders BCI to Act Against Law Students",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court of India ruled that the Bar Council of India (BCI) and state bar councils have no statutory power to regulate law students, citing that such regulation rests with universities. The court emphasized that students' legal rights and conduct are subject to the guidance of their universities.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court of India ordered the Bar Council of India (BCI) to have oversight by the Attorney General for India and the Solicitor General for India.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The SC ruled that the BCI and state bar councils have no legal authority to act against law students.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The BCI's jurisdiction over law students begins only after they register as advocates under the Advocates Act, 1961.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
